 "notes": [
  "Every live board master is listed. Matching is on the board CODE printed in the Board column, verified against grade + GSM + sheet size; 328 of 329 matched by code with zero attribute drift.",
  "Rows are set to the sheet figure absolutely (target minus on hand), not added. Boards already at the sheet figure are untouched.",
  "A difference under 1 sheet is ignored: the sheet stores packets to 2 decimals, so a carried-over ERP figure such as 19,400 sheets reads back as 134.72 pkt = 19,399.68 and would otherwise shave a third of a sheet.",
  "The three Paper grades carry no sheets_per_packet by design, so packets cannot be converted. All three read 0 on the sheet and hold 0, so nothing is lost by skipping them.",
  "RESOLVED 2026-07-31 by Anik: 3032300SAFF (Saffire 300 30x31.5) is 15 packets, final. The 30x31 row was a TYPO - a duplicate row for this same board, not a second lot - so its 90 packets were never real stock. The board goes to 15, and the 90 is written off rather than carried.",
  "IGNORED: 3031300SAFF - the duplicate row created by that mis-typed size. Its master was deleted on 31 Jul; what it appeared to hold is this same board counted twice."
